Launch qa agent with quality skill to test task {{.task_id}}: "{{.title}}".
{{- if ne .priority "0"}}
PRIORITY: {{.priority}}/10.
{{- end}}

LOAD: quality skill.

READ:
(1) Task spec at {{.file_path}}
(2) Feature test plan (09-test-plan.md) for the acceptance test cases mapped to this task
(3) Feature PRD for feature-level intent
(4) Implementation code and test results{{if .files_changed}} (files: {{.files_changed}}){{end}}
{{- if .related_docs}}
(5) Related docs: {{.related_docs}}
{{- end}}
{{- if .related_tasks}}
({{if .related_docs}}6{{else}}5{{end}}) Related tasks: {{.related_tasks}}
{{- end}}
{{- if .depends_on}}
DEPENDENCIES: {{.depends_on}} — verify these tasks are completed before proceeding.
{{- end}}

VALIDATE:
- Run test cases from feature test plan that map to this task
- Verify acceptance criteria are met per the feature test plan, not just the task spec
- Check edge cases identified in the test plan
- Validate integration points behave correctly

E2E REACHABILITY VERIFICATION (Step 5.5):
- Confirm all new code has call sites from the runtime entry point, not just unit tests
- Trace from application main/startup through to every new function or component
- If any new code is unreachable from the runtime entry point, FAIL the QA check
- Document the call chain for each new component in the QA report

CODEX RED-TEAM VERIFICATION (Step 5.7):
- Run an independent codex cross-check of the implementation against the spec
- Codex findings OVERRIDE Claude's assessment — if codex identifies a gap, it is a failure
- See quality/workflows/qa-testing.md for detailed codex red-team procedure
- This step is MANDATORY — do not skip even if all other checks pass
- If codex is unavailable or fails to run, mark the task as blocked rather than passing

ON PASS (all test cases pass, acceptance criteria met):
- Add note: shark note add --task={{.task_id}} --type=review "QA passed - all test cases validated"
- Advance: {{template "advance" .}}

ON FAIL (test cases fail, acceptance criteria not met, regressions found):
- Add note with specific failures: shark note add --task={{.task_id}} --type=blocker "QA failed - [describe failures]"
- Send back to development: shark task update {{.task_id}} --status=ready_for_development
- Do NOT use any invented status. The valid rejection status from QA is ready_for_development.
